   "replies": [
    " 20 is low and relatively small. 23 - 45 = -22. I should try multiplying by 2 to make 6 more reasonable. To equal 20 and my target number 6, I could use 6 fours: 4 * 4 + 4 = 20. So, <answer> (23 - 45) / 4 </answer>",
    " HasBeenSet that the result is 20 is odd and relatively small. The largest number is 48 and for an equation to be divisible by 48 the starting number must be divisible by 48. 48 / 23 = 2.08, which does not equal a whole number. The next possible starting number is 45.  \u0441\u043b\u0443\u0447\u0430\u044f\u0445 45 / 48 = 0.94, also not a whole number. The next possible starting number is 23. \u65cf\u81ea\u6cbb\u5dde 23 / 48 = 4.81, not a whole number either. The only surviving starting number is 45. j\u0105cych bu\u1ed9c thi\u1ebft 48 - END.\n\u6811\u7acb <answer> 48 - 23 - \u00d7 45 </answer>.",
